From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asuvath <asuvath.monikandan@adlinktech.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6dsp-lpass-clocks: set drvdata before registering
 clocks

q6dsp_clock_dev_probe() adds the OF clock provider before it sets
drvdata, but the clock ops get their struct q6dsp_cc from
dev_get_drvdata(). A consumer probing in that window, such as the LPASS
LPI pinctrl, can prepare a clock while drvdata is still NULL and
dereferences NULL in clk_vote_q6dsp_block(). This happens with the clk
prepare_lock held, so later clock users block and the boot stalls.

Set drvdata before any clock is registered.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -147,6 +147,9 @@
 	cc->dev = dev;
 	q6dsp_clks = desc->clks;
 
+	/* the clk ops read cc from drvdata: set it before any clock is visible */
+	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_clks; i++) {
 		unsigned int id = q6dsp_clks[i].clk_id;
 		struct clk_init_data init = {
@@ -179,8 +182,6 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6dsp_clock_dev_probe);
